  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Authentication (Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server.Auth), two additions to the cookie login of the templates.\nExternal logins: sign in with Microsoft Entra ID, Google, AWS Cognito or any OpenID Connect provider. IExternalLoginProvider with EntraLoginProvider / GoogleLoginProvider / CognitoLoginProvider / OidcLoginProvider, each taking its own settings class (the same shape as IMailSender / IFileStorage); the application lists the configured providers in a table (ExternalLoginTable in the templates) and passes them to AddExternalLogins(...). The verified identity is mapped to a user row by the application's IExternalLoginUserResolver, so authorization (user module, UserRead/Write conditions) is unchanged. Includes per-provider validation (Entra UPN / guest rejection / issuer format for multi-tenant, verified e-mail for Google and Cognito, allowed domains), two-step logout that also ends the IdP session, and a one-time ticket flow for native (MAUI) clients that sign in through the system browser. See docs/ExternalLogin.md.\nTOTP two-factor authentication (RFC 6238) for the ID/password login: TotpLogin verifies the authenticator code after the password check, enrolls on first login (QR code via QRCoder), keeps the secret in the three write-only columns declared on LoginAccountContractField (no DDL is issued) and rejects reused codes. See docs/TwoFactorLogin.md.\nLoginAccountStore: the login-time access to the user table (verify ID/password, resolve an external identity to an account, reject inactive accounts, create the initial administrator). Table and columns come from the current-user module design: IdField and LoginAccountContractField (login ID / external match / active flag / display name / password hash and salt columns, which are optional for IdP-only apps). Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.8.3.\nEmailOtpLogin: two-factor login by a 6-digit one-time code sent by e-mail (enabled by the TwoFactorEmail role of LoginAccountContractField; codes live in IDistributedCache with an expiry and an attempt limit, no columns needed). The template sends through MailDispatcher. See docs/TwoFactorLogin.md.\nOidcLoginProvider: rejects an e-mail login name whose email_verified claim is false, and always requests the openid scope even when Scopes leaves it out.",
